  "date": "11 October 2026",
  "summary_en": "The Polar To UV node converts polar coordinates (distance and angle from an origin) into Cartesian coordinates, output as a uv layer or attribute. It recalculates each pixel's value in place and does not relocate pixels by itself.",
  "inputs": [
    "angle (optional): layer or attribute setting how far around the origin each point rotates",
    "length (optional): layer or attribute setting each point's distance from the origin"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Signature: layer type accepted by the source",
    "Angle Units: Radians (unit circle), Degrees or Circles (0 to 1, where a full turn is 1)",
    "Angle: fallback angle when no angle input is wired",
    "Length: fallback distance from the origin when no length input is wired",
    "Output: uv, the Cartesian coordinates"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Does not move pixels by itself. To relocate pixels, chain UV Map COP, then Polar to UV COP, then UV Sample COP."
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Polar To UV convertit des coordonnées polaires en coordonnées UV cartésiennes, sans déplacer les pixels : il faut le chaîner avec UV Map et UV Sample."
}
